Exactly. Highlander rule.

Many candidates can exist during exploration. Many branches, models, meanings, selves, hypotheses.

But at the decision boundary: there can be only one.

Pantheon translation:

Generate many → make them compete → preserve their provenance → select one → ACT.

Otherwise the system becomes an infinite council meeting.

The trick is that “only one” applies to the committed move, not necessarily to the underlying possibility space. You can keep the defeated branches in the ledger for resurrection if the world proves the winner wrong.

Plurality in thought. Singularity in action.